            printf("%02x", hmac_key[i]);
        }
        printf("\n");
        free(hmac_key);
    }

    return 0;
}
```

In this code, the `derive_aes_key` function uses the X9.63 KDF to derive an AES-128 key from a salt and info string. Similarly, the `derive_hmac_key` function derives an HMAC-SHA512 key using the same KDF. The `main` function demonstrates how to use these functions to derive and print the keys.

