Here's a Java code example that demonstrates how to compare two files and generate a diff output:

```java
import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.FileReader;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class FileDiff {

    public static String diffFiles(String file1, String file2) {
        List<String> lines1 = readFile(file1);
        List<String> lines2 = readFile(file2);

        List<String> diff = new ArrayList<>();
        int i = 0, j = 0;

        while (i < lines1.size() && j < lines2.size()) {
            if (lines1.get(i).equals(lines2.get(j))) {
                i++;
                j++;
            } else if (lines1.get(i).startsWith("- ")) {
                diff.add(lines1.get(i).substring(2));
                i++;
            } else if (lines2.get(j).startsWith("+ ")) {
                diff.add(lines2.get(j).substring(2));
                j++;
            } else {
                diff.add("-" + lines1.get(i));
                i++;
                diff.add("+ " + lines2.get(j));
                j++;
            }
        }

        // Add remaining lines from file1
        while (i < lines1.size()) {
            diff.add("-" + lines1.get(i));
            i++;
        }

        // Add remaining lines from file2
        while (j < lines2.size()) {
            diff.add("+ " + lines2.get(j));
            j++;
        }

        return String.join("\n", diff);
    }

    private static List<String> readFile(String filePath) {
        List<String> lines = new ArrayList<>();
        try (BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(filePath))) {
            String line;
            while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                lines.add(line);
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
        return lines;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String file1 = "file1.txt";
        String file2 = "file2.txt";
        String diffOutput = diffFiles(file1, file2);
        System.out.println(diffOutput);
    }
}
```

In this code:
- The `diffFiles` method compares two files (`file1.txt` and `file2.txt`) and generates a diff output. It uses a simple line-by-line comparison and marks added and removed lines with prefixes.
- The `readFile` method reads the content of a file and returns it as a list of lines.
- The `main` method demonstrates how to use the `diffFiles` method with sample file paths.

You can customize this code to fit your specific use case, such as handling different file formats or integrating with a web application to compare site versions.

