- JavaScript:
    - Retrieves the input elements and the result/chart canvas.
    - Calculates the markup amount and total price based on user input.
    - Displays the result in the `result` div.
    - Uses the Chart.js library to create a bar chart representing the cost, markup, and total price.

**5. Include Chart.js:**

Make sure to include the Chart.js library by adding the following script tag in your HTML file:

```html
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js"></script>
```

This will fetch the Chart.js library from a CDN, making it available for use in your JavaScript code.

**6. Test and Run:**

Open the `index.html` file in a web browser to see your Markup Calculator in action. You can input different values and see the results displayed both as text and on the chart.

Remember to customize the styling and add more features as needed for your specific use case. This project provides a solid foundation for a markup calculator with charting capabilities.

